Also drops -Werror=return-type: ceres-solver's bundled miniglog shim
(ceres/internal/miniglog/glog/logging.h) doesn't mark its FATAL-log
codepath as [[noreturn]], so GCC 15 flags "control reaches end of non-void
function" at every LOG(FATAL)-terminated function in cartographer's own
code that expands through it. A CXXFLAGS-level -Wno-error=return-type
doesn't win here: GOOG_CXX_FLAGS's own -Werror=return-type is appended to
the per-target compile command *after* CXXFLAGS, so it always overrides a
CXXFLAGS-level override. Same "vendored third-party header bug, not
cartographer's" reasoning as the pre-existing -Werror=uninitialized removal
above -- fixing it at the actual source avoids the ordering problem
entirely.

